Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    LOW GRADE ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS   SEE NOTE   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST   NEW MARGIN   EXCISION   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue with short stitch posteriorly  2 pins  long stitch   1 pin  laterally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm ill defined tan white  firm mass that abuts the lateral margin  Representative section of tumor at the closest  lateral  margin is frozen as FX 1 and the is submitted in cassette A  The extreme posterior margin is submitted in cassette B and the next adjacent section is submitted in cassette C  The posterior margin is double inked with green color and the anterior margin inked black in cassette C   The tumor closest to the closest margin  lateral  is submitted in cassette D  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  new margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Long stitch is in the lateral side and the short stitch in the superior side  The old margin is inked in black and the new lateral margin is inked in blue  The superior margin is inked in red  Representative section taken through the old margin and the new margins are presented in cassettes E G  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                              