 sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a potential node  The specimen is quadrisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show focally moderate overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Note  Immunohistochemical stains for kappa and lambda light chain demonstrate a polytypic population of plasma cells in the sentinel lymph node  Scattered plasma cells express IgM  but they are a small minority of the overall plasma cell population  These results do not confirm the presence of involvement by the patient s known marginal zone B cell lymphoma  However  the node remains suspicious for involvement based on the histologic features  i e   a lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate composed of numerous plasma cells showing occasional slightly immature nuclei and rare Dutcher bodies  and monocytoid lymphocytes with slightly irregular nuclei infiltrating germinal centers  If clinically indicated  additional studies could be performed for a more defin