Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Nash  Jennifer Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  Two satellite nodules by MRI inferior and anterior to main mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH AREAS OF SPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA  METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The spindle cell component demonstrates greater cellularity  mitotic activity  and pleomorphism than that typically seen in reactive stroma  The spindle cells are focally positive for cytokeratin AEI 3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 and show focal  weak staining for wide spectrum cytokeratin  they are largely negative for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   These findings are consistent with the diagnosis of a spindle cell carcinoma component  The tumor cells are negative for GCDFP 15 and nuclear WT 1  The latter result  in conjunction with the presence of an in situ component  supports a breast origin for this tumor  All three nodules show a similar histology  A prominent  dense lymphocytic response is present  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Three nodules   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm Grade  3 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of the ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL  SUPERIOR TO LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  RARE ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS PRESENT IN 1 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SENTINEL LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  4 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Method of detection  Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan yellow fibrofatty breast excision specimen  There is a short stitch designating superior and a long lateral  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  On sectioning  three separate masses are identified  The largest superior mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm and is ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  coming to 0 4cm from the posterior  1 0cm from the medial  1 2cm from the superior  1 4cm from the anterior  1 6cm from the lateral  and 3 1cm from the inferior margins  Located 1 5cm inferior is another ill defined  tan pink and focally hemorrhagic  indurated mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  This mass is 0 5cm from the posterior  0 8cm from the medial  1 2cm from both the anterior and the lateral  1 0cm from the inferior and 4 6cm from the superior margins  The third indurated  ill defined mass is located at the anterolateral aspect  mea