AME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  re excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan white ellipse of skin  The specimen is not oriented  There is a linear  well healed surgical incision on the skin surface which measures 3 0cm  The margins are marked with black ink  The isthmus is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm in diameter biopsy cavity which open to the nearest margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm soft  tan  ovoid nodule adjacent to the cavity  which extends to 0 2cm of the nearest margin  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of intervening soft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY    INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  NO PERINEURAL  LYMPHATIC OR VASCULAR INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  SEE NOTE    ONE OF ONE INTRAMAMMARY LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  NOTE  No in situ component is identified  The carcinoma is extensively present on many slides  The gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm semifirm white focus 0 2cm from an inked margin  The lesion is too small to freeze  The lesion is submitted in cassettes A through C  remainder in cassettes D through I  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Daniel Brian Hoch  M D  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Checked.
