Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  MASS  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION EXTENDING TO THE INKED DEEP AND LATERAL RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROADENOMA  0 2 CM   NOTE  No blood vessel or lymphatic invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  METASTATIC BREAST CARCINOMA TO SEVEN OUT OF EIGHT LYMPH NODES  WITH FOCAL EXTENSION INTO AXILLARY ADIPOSE TISSUE  BREAST   ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST   ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 19 06 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast with needle  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow fibroadipose tissue with a suture marking the deep margin and a localizing wire noted by the surgeon to be the anterior lateral point of the specimen  The resection margins are inked as follows  Inferior   blue  superior   black  deep   red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregularly shaped firm white mass with stellate extension that comes to within 0 2cm from the inferior and the superior resection margin  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  C and D are from the same slice divided in the middle   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Superior margin  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes E  F  and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes H through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s na