5cm tan pink skin ellipse  The surface shows a 3 5cm linear scar 1 7cm lateral to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unremarkable tan pink nipple  The resection margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic cavity in the mid portion of the specimen which comes to 1 1cm of the deep margin  There is surrounding dense gray pink fibrous tissue up to 2 0cm with no suspicious induration or other gross abnormality  The remaining mammary tissue is 60  gray white fibrous and 40  tan yellow lobular adipose tissue  Sectioning of the probable upper outer quadrant reveals multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Cavity to deep margin C  Cavity to superficial margin D  Cavity to skin E  Cavity F G  Fibrous tissue away from cavity H  Lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm simple mastectomy specimen  with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan pink skin ellipse  The surface shows a 5 0cm healed scar which arises 3cm superio lateral to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm unremarkable tan pink nipple  The margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm hemorrhagic cavity arising in the portion of the specimen which comes to 0 5cm of deep margin and is surrounded by focally bright yellow orange dense gray white fibrous tissue up to 2 0cm with no induration or other gross abnormality  The remaining mammary tissue is 40  dense gray white fibrous tissue and 60  tan yellow lobular adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  I N  Cavity to deep margin O P  Dense fibrous tissue away from cavity Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                  