ion  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 99 at 15 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary node contents   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 2 5cm mastectomy with an attached REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 5cm axillary tail and an overlying a REMOVED_DATE X 13 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 0cm ill defined  pink to tan  gritty  irregular mass in the upper inner quadrant which extends to 2 1cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin  2 0cm from the medial margin  10 5cm from the lateral margin  3 7cm from the superior margin  and 8 0cm from the inferior margin  A section of the mass with closest posterior margin is submitted in cassette A  The entire mass is submitted in cassettes B  J K and M P  A second ill defined  firm 2 x 1 x 1cm area is identified in the upper outer quadrant  A representative section of this area is submitted in cassette C  An additional section of this area with closest posterior margin is submitted in L  Representative sections of firm breast tissue lateral to this area are submitted in U W  Further sectioning of specimen reveals a firm REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 1cm nodule in the lower outer quadrant which is decalcified and submitted in Cassette X  The attached axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple gray tan lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest diameter  They are submitted in D I  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
