ion margin  and 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The tumor mass  3 is 0 7cm in greatest dimension  is approximately at 6 o clock  3cm from the anterior resection margin  1cm from the posterior resection margin  and 0 8cm from the tumor mass  2  The tumor mass  4 is approximately at 10 o clock  and it measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and it is 2cm from the posterior resection margin  and 2 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The tumor mass  4 is rubbery and well circumscribed  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly multifibrotic  No other lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  1  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma between tumor mass  1 and tumor mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the tumor mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  3  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma between tumor mass  2 and tumor mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  4  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma between tumor mass  2 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the masses  medially  at 3cm from the larger tumor mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the tumor masses  at 3 5cm from the larger one  laterally   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five representative sections of tissue near the axillary region  query axillary nodes   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right mastectomy flap   are four unoriented fragments of skin measuring 13 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm respectively  All four fragmented skin specimens appear grossly unremarkable  A representative section of each of them is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  F