 T  McKee MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tumor   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch indicating inferior  and a long stitch indicating lateral  and bow tie indicating cephalad  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior black  posterior blue  and superior orange  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm spiculated  hard mass  1 0cm from the superior margin  0 8cm from the inferior margin  1 0cm from the anterior margin  0 7cm from the posterior margin  2 8cm from the medial margin  and 2 5cm from the lateral margin  The remainder of the specimen is fibrofatty and has no masses or lesions identified  SECTION CODE  A  Mass with anterior and posterior margins  B C  Mass with anterior and posterior margins  D  Mass with superior and inferior margins  E H  Representative sections of unremarkable breast tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right primary sentinel node  631  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette R  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right secondary sentinel  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left primary sentinel node  617  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette T  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left secondary sentinel node  62  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm lymph node entirely submitted in cassette U  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm portion of breast tissue which is oriented by the surgeon with a short suture designating  anterior   a long suture designating  lateral   and a bow tie suture designating  cephalad   There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined  tan white to pink firm mass  which comes to 1 0cm from both the anterior and posterior margin  The mass is greater than 2 0cm from the remaining margins  1 5cm from the mass is a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  tan white mass  which comes to within 0 5cm from inferior margin  The fibrous tissue directly surrounding the mass is indurated with dilated ducts filled with a white material  The remaining breast parenchyma is approximately 70  yellow lobular adipose and 30  of dense white fibrous tissue  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue and the superior green  Representative sections are submitted as follows  I J   tumor to posterior margin  K L   tumor to anterior margin  M N   surrounding indurated fibrous tissue with dilated ducts  0 5cm to anterior margin  O P   smaller  second tumor to inferior margin  Q   fibrous parenchyma to superior margin  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  BREAST MASS  MARGINS GROSSLY NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  LUMPECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODE RIGHT PRIMARY SENTINEL 631  EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE RIGHT SECONDARY SENTINEL 174  EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE LEFT PRIMARY SENTINEL 617  EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODE LEFT SECONDARY SENTINEL 62  EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SEVERAL FOCI  AGGREGATING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free from invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 AUG 98 at 08 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a red pink  stellate region measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and extending grossly to within 0 3cm of the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassettes A  Sections B through D are representative sections of the tumor  C D tumor nearest margin   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the tumor is submitted in cassette E  Other sections are in F J  Gross Description by  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST   EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH AREA HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASION  O R  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
