Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 18 03 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  FORMING SEVERAL NODULES THAT SPAN REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADE LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MEDIAL  SUPERIOR  AND LATERAL MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL INFERIOR ASPECT    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ABUTTING THE FINAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The final margin of the specimen appears free of invasive carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY CAVITY    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm fibroadipose tissue with indicating wire  The specimen is inked as follows  black superior  red inferior  blue lateral  green medial  yellow deep  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white area of irregular borders that is 0 5cm from closest  inferior  red  margin and 1 0cm from the superior  black  margin  The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A I  with firm area in cassettes C  D and E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  are three portions of adipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Sectioning reveals two lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Each lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted  the smaller lymph node in cassette J  and the larger lymph nodes in K L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  is a REMOVE