Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 54 year old woman with a history of invasive ductal carcinoma undergoing excision and sentinel lymph node biopsy  A second area of architectural distortion is also excised by needle localization  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY 1  RADIAL SCAR  EXTENSIVE 2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE  C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT   SENTINEL    EXCISION METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  1 1   SEE TABLE 2 AND NOTE  D  BREAST  LEFT ANTERIOR  MARGIN   EXCISION FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  SEE NOTE  E  BREAST  LEFT POSTERIOR  MARGIN   EXCISION FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  SEE NOTE  F  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR  MARGIN   EXCISION FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  SEE NOTE  G  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   DISSECTION FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES WITH NO TUMOR IDENTIFIED  0 15   SEE TABLE 2 AND NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  0 7cm  microscopic measurement  The invasive carcinoma is present in association with a healing biopsy site  GRADE  REMOVED_DATE LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measures 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  16 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Note  Due to an issue with fixation and tissue processing in this case  the histologic findings and immunohistochemical staining results are limited  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern is limited due to sectioning artifact and lack of staining in several sections  however  the myoepithelial layer is highlighted in a few areas of the radial scar and supports the diagnosis  Similarly  immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on nine tissue levels of the sentinel lymph node  part C  failed to show appropriate staining and are interpreted as non contributory  The diagnosis of metastatic ductal carcinoma is based on the H E stained sections  Dr  Fritz Koerner and Dr  David Wilbur have reviewed the slides for part A and concur with the diagnosis of radial scar  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast needle biopsy   is a 6 x 4 x 2 5cm oriented breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral and localization wire in place  The long axis of the specimen is going from medial to lateral and the specimen is inked as follows  Anterior  Blue  Posterior  Black  Superior  Green  and Inferior  Yellow  Upon sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm white stellar area which is 0 9cm from the medial end margin  0 5cm from the superior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin  0 7cm from the inferior margin  1 2cm from the anterior margin  and 3 5cm from the lateral end margin  The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion closest to the superior  anterior  and inferior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior and additional inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest superior margin with the extension of the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior and inferior margins closest to the scar area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end margin  en face  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left lumpectomy with repair   is an 8 x 5 x 2cm oriented piece of breast tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior  The long axis is medial to lateral and specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  and inferior   yellow  Upon sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm biopsy cavity with a granulated firm tan surface  The cavity abuts the anterior margin  is 0 5cm from the superior margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  and 1 3cm from the inferior margin  1 0cm from the medial end margin  and 3 5cm from the lateral end margin  The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire residual resection cavity and closest margin are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The section neighboring to the biopsy cavity  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A section of breast parenchyma away from the lesion  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Howland  REMOVE_MRN and  left sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node which is bisected and half is frozen as FX  1  now entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of the entirely submitted positive lymph node are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 4 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left anterior margin   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with a stitch demarcating new margin  The new margin is inked black and specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left posterior breast margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of oriented fibroadipose tissue  with a stitch demarcating the new margin  The new margin is inked black and specimen is serially sectioned and is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left superior breast margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 0cm fibroadipose tissue oriented with a stitch designating the new margin  The new margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   is a 12 x 6 x 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue  unoriented  The specimen is sectioned and numerous candidate lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA  INVOLVING MOST OF THE LYMPH NODE  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 27 49PM By his her