s not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 07 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy specimen weighing 560 grams and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm  There is a stitch denoting the 12 o clock position of the specimen  The anterior skin surface measures REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm with a nipple areola complex measuring 2 5cm in diameter  The nipple appears diffusely ulcerated and erythematous  However  there is no mass grossly identified underneath the nipple  The nipple is cross sectioned to reveal scattered underlying hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections of the ulcerated nipple are submitted in cassettes A B  The entire resected surface is black inked and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm mass at 12 o clock adjacent to  but not involving intact breast prosthesis  The breast mass is irregularly circumscribed  gritty  tan  and firm and is approximately 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  The mass is approximately 2 2cm from the closest posterior margin  Representative sections of the mass and the anterior margin are submitted into cassettes C F  A representative section of the closest posterior margin to this mass is submitted into cassette G  Further sectioning reveals a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregularly circumscribed breast mass present at the 11 o clock posterior portion of the specimen  This mass appears to approach the posterior margin to within 0 2cm  Representative sections of this mass with the closest posterior margin are submitted into cassettes H I and representative sections of this mass with the closest anterior margin are submitted into cassettes J K  There is also an irregular thickening of the breast at the 1 o clock posterior region which measures approximately 1 6cm in maximal dimension  Representative sections of this region are submitted into cassettes L N  Serial sectioning of the breast parenchyma surrounding the implant reveals a diffuse firm and white nodularity to the breast parenchyma with scattered calcification  The surface of the implant is white yellow  and focally calcified and firm  A representative section of a focally brown and firm nodular region at 2 o clock is submitted into cassette O  A focal region at approximately 8 o clock in the specimen shows a bulbous protrusion of the breast implant without any adjacent reaction in the fibrofatty breast parenchyma  A representative section of the unremarkable breast parenchyma at 9 o clock is submitted into cassette P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty and lymphoid tissue with multiple enlarged lymph nodes  the largest grossly measuring 1 6cm in maximal dimension  Representative individual candidate lymph nodes are submitted into cassettes Q W  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    WITH TUBULAR FEATURES  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION SLIDE   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  ADJACENT TO  BUT NOT DISTANT FROM  INFILTRATING TUMOR  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  CYSTS AND FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  4  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS OF ARTERIES  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a breast biopsy containing a 1 1cm in greatest diameter stellate  firm  tan mass approaching an inked margin  Representative tissue is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in A  remainder of mass in B through D with representative surrounding in E through G  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND CRIBRIFORM DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
