Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 03 CLINICAL DATA  Pre op chemotherapy patient  positive left breast axillary node                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 2 OF 28 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2 AND SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin immunostains confirm the presence of metastatic carcinoma cells in the lymph nodes  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  1 2cm as measured on a glass slide   see note   Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  2  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested  NOTE  The invasive tumor appears multifocal and this multifocally makes accurate assessment of size difficult  Although the tumor spans 1 2cm on a glass slide  it may exceed 2 0cm  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  2  Number of lymph nodes examined  28  see note   Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  1  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Note  The metastatic tumor is identified in hematoxylin and eosin stained slides as well as keratin immunostained slides  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 53                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast and axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a overlying elliptical portion of tan white skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm  NO scar is grossly appreciated  The nipple areolar complex measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm and a tan pink unremarkable centrally located nipple  There is a stitch designating the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  Along the posterior aspect are two reddish brown unremarkable portions of skeletal muscle measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm well delineated dense tan pink rubbery fibrotic area located within the mid portion of the specimen  coming to 1 0cm from the posterior and 1 5cm from the skin surface  Within the most superior portion of fibrotic area is an ill defined  indurated area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and coming to 2 2cm from the posterior and 2 5cm from the overlying skin  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink  lobulated unremarkable breast tissue with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  Within the axillary tail multiple tan pink rubbery lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Posterior overlying margin of indurated irregular area  B E  Representative sections of indurated ill defined irregular area  F G  Representative section of surrounding dense fibrous tissue  H  Four whole lymph nodes  I  Five whole lymph nodes  J  Six whole lymph nodes  K  One bisected lymph node  L  One bisected lymph node  M  One bisected lymph node  N  Four whole lymph nodes  O  Six whole lymph nodes  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA  Known breast cancer reviewed at Brigham and Women s Hospital  invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Scattered tumor cells   25  are detected on cytokeratin immunostains only  a total of 3 stains examined   The involved lymph node measures 1 3cm  and extranodal involvement is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE AND IN SITU MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma is predominately lobular in its morphology  but there are focal areas of cohesion and polarization  An E cadherin stain demonstrates predominately only cytoplasmic staining of these in situ tumor cells  but in the focal cohesive areas  membranous staining is noted  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain shows strong cytoplasmic staining  Together  these morphologic and immunohistochemical findings are consistent with an in situ carcinoma with both lobular and ductal features  As the invasive component is morphologically similar to the in situ component  it is also classified as having features of both lobular and ductal carcinoma  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Main 2 5cm mass and multiple satellite nodules  aggregating to at least 3cm in total  Tumor extends into the dermis  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Grade of in situ carcinoma  3  Location of in situ carcinoma  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Margin of in situ carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXICSION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 20 29                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block G   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Some tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a 1 3cm tan pink lymph node which is bivalved to reveal a tan pink unremarkable cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now submitted as A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 310 gram  REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm right simple mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm possible axillary tail in the upper outer quadrant  The black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm tan pink skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm indurated nodular area  possible flattened nipple  which comes to 0 5cm from the lower outer skin margin  Extending medially from the indurated area is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar which comes to 0 9cm of the lower inner skin margin  The resection margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm stellate gray white tumor mass with focal hemorrhage and bright yellow orange areas  contiguous with the indurated skin lesion and arising in the mid portion of the specimen  The mass comes to 3 2cm of the deep  0 9cm of the inferior superficial and 1 2cm of the superior superficial margin  Centrally the mass shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous biopsy site  Between the mass and the deep margin are multiple firm tan white nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The former comes to 1 0cm from the deep margin and the remaining nodules are  2 0cm from the deep margin  The remaining tissue is composed of 40  dense gray white fibrous tissue and 60  tan yellow adipose tissue  The fibrous tissue is focally gritty  Sectioning of the possible axillary tail reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B C  Deep margin closest to tumor and satellite nodules D  Firm tan white nodules between tumor and deep margin E  Tumor to inferior superficial margin F  Tumor to superior superficial margin G H  Tumor with hemorrhagic biopsy cavity I  Tumor J K  Focally gritty fibrous tissue away from tumor Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast skin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm strip of unremarkable tan pink skin  The margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as L  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION , Unchecked.
