ion of tan pink fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the lateral yellow  and the medial green  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fairly well defined  gray white to pink red indurated  stellate mass within an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm hemorrhagic focus consistent with pervious biopsy site  The mass abuts the posterior margin  and comes to 0 4cm of the medial  1 0cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the superior  1 8cm of the anterior  and 2 1cm of the lateral margin  The remaining cut surface shows focally dense gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved breast tissue superior to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor to closest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section of i inferior margin including closest approach of tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  en face   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  609   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan red lymph node with a minimal amount of attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional margin lateral   inferior left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portio of gray white to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the new inferior margin  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The new inferior margin is inked black  The anterior rim is over inked green  and the posterior rim over inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to later