Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Aliyah Rahemtullah  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1 AND SEE NOTE   2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  gross measurements   GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Positive at the antero superior margin of the specimen in one focus  is less than 0 1cm from the lateral margin along a broad front  and is 0 2cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  multiple levels examined  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  with comedonecrosis  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the antero superior and latero superior margins of the specimen in one focus  is 0 15cm from the antero medial margin in one focus  and is 0 2cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  multiple levels examined  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Not indicated  see prior report MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Both the invasive ductal carcinoma and the ductal carcinoma in situ are surrounded by an extensive and dense lymphoid infiltrate  Immunostains highlight numerous B cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  in follicles in normal distribution  The germinal centers are Bcl 2 negative and Bcl 6 positive   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative  but may be technically suboptimal  T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  are in a normal interfollicular distribution  The nodular meshwork of the follicular dendritic cells is  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  Ki67 shows a high proliferative rate with polarization in the reactive follicles  Kappa and lambda light chains by in situ hybridization show normal polyclonal plasma cells  Overall  the morphological and immunohistochemical findings are consistent with a reactive peritumoral process  Dr  N L  Harris reviewed the slides and concurs with the interpretation  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  BOTH INVOLVING 1 OF 4 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  SEE NOTE   2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunostains for keratin  calponin  myosin  and p63 support the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  INVOLVING 2 OF 3 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple levels examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE 