strogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams  24 x 20 x 4cm right simple mastectomy with a stitch which designates the 12 o clock margin  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The overlying  semicircular  18 x 11 5cm light tan skin ellipse has six round uniformly tan brown pigmented lesions that range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  The skin is otherwise grossly unremarkable  The 3 x 3cm nipple areolar complex is grossly unremarkable  No scars are identified  In the upper inner quadrant is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm area composed of firm  gritty  stellate white gray tissue  and an adjacent 1 x 1 x 1cm round well defined area with hemorrhage and calcification which could correspond to healing biopsy site  This lesion is located 1 8cm from the closest deep margin  2 4cm from the anterior margin and 5cm from the closest skin surface  The remaining breast is approximately 80  fatty tissue and 20  fibrous tissue  The fibrous tissue has focal areas of suspicious induration  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary portion of the specimen  Representative sections of the breast are submitted as follows  A E  Tissue below the nipple F J  Stellate lesion submitted entirely  cassette F lesion to closest deep margin   K M  Representative sections of fibrous areas in the remaining breast  N  Representative section of two largest pigmented lesions of the skin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 1 110 grams  27 x 20 x 4cm left simple mastectomy with a stitch designating the 12 o clock margin  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The overlying  semi circular  17 x 13 5cm ellipse of tan smooth skin which contains a 4 x 3 8cm mesoareolar complex  The mammary skin and nipple are grossly unremarkable  On cross section  the breast is approximately 70  fatty tissue and 30  fibrous tissue  The fibrous tissue is soft  has ill defined borders and does not form discrete lesions or masses  No lymph nodes are grossly identified in the axillary portion of the specimen  The tissue is submitted as follows  O X  Representative sections of the fibrous tissue submitted from the 12 o clock to the 6 o clock margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan rubbery piece of tissue with blue ink frozen entirely as FX  1  now submitted as Y  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan rubbery piece of tissue with blue ink frozen entirely as FX  2  now submitted as Z  Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  JOSHUA B  KISH  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UN