ns measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Extensive  corresponding to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm grossly visible lesion  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The foci of invasive carcinoma are small  which may limit accurate assessment of histologic grade  but the invasive tumor cells appear high grade  similar to the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  calponin  and myosin show that the foci of invasive carcinoma lack myoepithelial cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  each labeled  Harriett Young  REMOVE_MRN   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of tan soft tissue containing two lymph nodes  each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The two lymph nodes and the remaining soft tissue are frozen in toto as FX 1 and now resubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm nipple located 8 5cm from the superior margin oriented with a stitch  12 o clock  and 4 0cm from the medial margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a fibrofatty yellow to white breast parenchyma which is focally firm and grossly consistent with fibrocystic changes  Some of the breast tissue in the subareolar region is stained blue consistent with the sentinel lymph node dye procedure  Representative sections are taken as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative radial section from inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative radial section from superior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrous breast parenchyma located 4 0cm from medial margin and 4 0cm from inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of areola and adjacent anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section to posterior margin deep to the areola   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial section to anterior margin located 3 0cm from the lateral margin and 3 0cm from the inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of area with fibrocystic change located 2 0cm from lateral margin and 4 0cm from inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of area with fibrocystic change located 2 0cm from medial margin and 3 0cm from inferior margin  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm left breast mastectomy partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm nipple located 4 0cm from the 6 o clock  inferior  margin as indicated by the stitch and 4 0cm from the medial margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black and is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm poorly circumscribed tan  focally hemorrhagic mass located 0 5cm from the nearest anterior margin  0 7cm from the nearest posterior margin  3 6cm from the nearest lateral margin  and 6 0cm from the inferior margin  The mass is 1 5cm superior and lateral to the nearest areolar skin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma appears yellow to white  fibrofatty with focal possible fibrocystic changes  No additional discrete lesions or masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass including nearest anterior and posterior margins  from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the mass  no margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of lateral margin nearest the mass  taken radially    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of fibrocystic change located 1 0cm from superior margin and 2 0cm from lateral margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma at the inferior margin  taken en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of areolar skin to underlying fibrous tissue and adjacent anterior margin  Also received within the same container is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of grossly unremarkable red to yellow fatty soft tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a homogeneous cut surface  Representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   LEFT AXILLARY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain   1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over expression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  531  to chromosome 17 signals  75  in 40 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY   report_end  , Unchecked.
