Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 25 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast  positive fine needle aspiration for cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  LESS THAN 5  OF TUMOR   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GREATER THAN 95  OF TUMOR   CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  2  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The carcinoma in situ extends to an inked resection surface  The infiltrating carcinoma extends to within 0 2cm of an inked surface  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The infiltrating carcinoma is present only in the frozen section block  The intraductal component is multifocal  throughout the biopsy  however  the tumor mass that contains the focus of invasion is less than 0 8cm in greatest dimension  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  INVOLVING A LOBULE  2  THE EXAMINED BREAST PARENCHYMA  DEEP RESECTION MARGINS AND 21 OF 21 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  3  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH RECENT HEMORRHAGE  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 58 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in two separately labeled parts  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue with a stitch designating the tumor site  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ill defined  tan  slightly firm and granular mass that is present at the inked margin  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1  now A  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is soft  yellow white and unremarkable  The remainder of the mass is submitted in B through D  Representative sections of the biopsy is submitted in E and F  Received on the back bench   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 28 x 15 x 3 0cm right modified mastectomy specimen  The right breast is 19 x 15 x 3 0cm with an overlying skin ellipse which is 18 x 9cm  The skin ellipse contains a 0 8cm unremark