Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 11 10 CLINICAL DATA  52 y o  female  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy for bulky breast carcinoma with axillary node metastasis                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2  EXTENDING TO A LATERAL MARGIN ACROSS A BROAD FRONT  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO AN INFERIOR MARGIN AND TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF A DEEP MARGIN  OTHER MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN 3 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  THE LARGEST REPLACED NODE REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  FIVE EXTRANODAL NODULES OF TUMOR INFILTRATING FAT  THE LARGEST REMOVED_DATE CM  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ADIPOSE TISSUE WITH FOCAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 18 21                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast lumpectomy specimen  A long stitch marks the lateral  and a short stitch the superior margin  The specimen is inked black overall with additional colors as follows  inferior red  lateral orange  superior blue  anterior yellow  medial green and deep black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm spiculated yellow white mass that grossly abuts the lateral margin  The tumor closely approaches the deep margin  however  extended invasion is difficult to evaluate as the tumor infiltrates the fibrous tissue of the deep margin and becomes mixed with it  The remaining margins  anterior  medial  inferior and superior  are grossly free of tumor  The remaining breast shows fibrous tissue with cysts at the deep margin and predominantly yellow fatty tissue in all other areas  Representative sections submitted  A B  representative inferior margin  C F  representative lateral margin  G I  representative deep margin  J K  representative medial margin  L M  representative anterior margin  N O  superior margin  P Q  additional tumor  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mass of fibrofatty tissue identified in the requisition as right axillary contents  A firm tan white lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm is identified and a portion saved for Dr  Dennis Sgroi  Representative section submitted  R S  representative largest lymph node  T U  one lymph node bisected  V BB  lymph nodes and fat  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional lateral deep margins  is a mass of fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm which is sectioned to reveal yellow adipose tissue admixed with white tissue with no grossly suspicious areas  Representative sections submitted in cassettes CC GG  approximately 50  of tissue is submitted   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins  are multiple fragments of fatty tissue  in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Entirely submitted in HH PP  Resident  STACEY L  MIKESELL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  TUMOR GROSSLY ABUTS A LATERAL MARGIN AND EXTENDS TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST RIGHT AXILLA CONTENTS   PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION , Unchecked.
